e the initial hypothesis, the feature extraction results, and the modeling results into a structured decision (accept/reject hypothesis) and a scientific summary in Markdown.\n\n*   **Pass the Markdown report from the `result_reporter_agent` to the `latex_reporter_agent`.** This agent is required to fulfill the \"save it in latex\" command. It will convert the Markdown scientific summary into a LaTeX document and render it to a PDF file.\n\n**Team Members Not Used:** All available agents are required for this specific request. The `feature_extraction_agent` and `modeling_agent` perform the core analytical work, while the `result_reporter_agent` and `latex_reporter_agent` are essential for generating the final deliverable in the specified format.\n", "thinking": null, "images": null, "tool_name": null, "tool_calls": null}, {"role": "user", "content": "Please execute your feature extraction process. Here is the required input JSON: { \"hypothesis\": \"Image-based radiomic features extracted from the regions defined by the masks can predict the target label.\", \"image_dir\": \"C:/sbme 26/GP/refactored project/OHIF-Standalone/Backend/mas/memory/workspace/labels_data\", \"mask_dir\": \"C:/sbme 26/GP/refactored project/OHIF-Standalone/Backend/mas/memory/workspace/labels_data\", \"targets_csv\": \"C:/sbme 26/GP/refactored project/OHIF-Standalone/Backend/mas/memory/workspace/targets.csv\", \"target_column\": \"target\" }. Provide your exact output.", "thinking": null, "images": null, "tool_name": null, "tool_calls": null}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "thinking": null, "images": null, "tool_name": null, "tool_calls": [{"function": {"name": "PyRadiomicsFeatureExtractionTool", "arguments": {"feature_classes": "firstorder,shape,glcm,glrlm,glszm,ngtdm,gldm", "id_column": "ID", "image_dir": "C:/sbme 26/GP/refactored project/OHIF-Standalone/Backend/mas/memory/workspace/labels_data", "mask_dir": "C:/sbme 26/GP/refactored project/OHIF-Standalone/Backend/mas/memory/worksp