etc.) and pass them as an array.\nStep 2: Call the feature extraction tool (`extract_radiomic_features`) with correct parameters.\n        After this step, write the extracted features file path (CSV) into 'configuration.json' under key 'radiomics_features'.\nStep 3: Call the feature importance tool (`analyze_feature_importance`) using the features file from Step 2 as input.\n        Save the resulting top features CSV file path in the JSON under key 'top_10_features'.\nStep 4: After completing all steps, provide a concise summary confirming successful execution and all updated JSON entries.\n\nYou MUST ensure that the 'configuration.json' file always reflects the latest outputs from each stage of the pipeline.\n", "thinking": null, "images": null, "tool_name": null, "tool_calls": null}, {"role": "user", "content": "The segmentation task has been completed successfully. Now I'll proceed with the next steps in your radiomics research study pipeline:\n\n1. **Segmentation** - \u2705 Complete\n2. **Feature Extraction** - Need to run the feature extraction agent\n3. **Modeling** - Need to run the modeling agent  \n4. **Report Generation** - Need to generate and save in LaTeX format\n\nHowever, I'm currently limited to only the segmentation tool. To continue with the full radiomics research study pipeline, you would need to:\n\n1. Run the feature extraction agent using the segmentation outputs:\n   - `image_dir`: \"C:/sbme 26/GP/refactored project/OHIF-Standalone/Backend/mas/memory/workspace/labels_data\"\n   - `mask_dir`: \"C:/sbme 26/GP/refactored project/OHIF-Standalone/Backend/mas/memory/workspace/labels_data\" \n   - `target_csv`: \"C:/sbme 26/GP/refactored project/OHIF-Standalone/Backend/mas/memory/workspace/targets.csv\"\n   - `target_label_name`: \"target\"\n\n2. Then run the modeling agent with the extracted features\n\n3. Finally generate the LaTeX report with the modeling results\n\nWould you like me to help you structure the commands or parameters for the next